      "reason": "Hobbes's experience of the violence during the English Civil War directly shaped the arguments for absolute sovereignty presented in his work Leviathan.",
      "evidence": "After returning to England from France in 1637, Hobbes witnessed the destruction and brutality of the English Civil War from 1642 to 1651 between Parliamentarians and Royalists, which heavily influenced his advocacy for governance by an absolute sovereign in Leviathan, as the solution to human conflict and societal breakdown.",
      "work": "Leviathan"
    }
  ]
}

